{"sourceSha256": "adeefa3820eed3eddb3dcb77967f46b893070b2120e0a88be11cdedce172e4db", "text": "Dear Doctor Smith,\nRe: Mrs. Sterra Fredrick, DOB 08/02/19\n\n| am writing to discharge one of your elderly patients back into your care. Mrs Frederick was\n\nadmitted to our Emergency Department following a fall and a suspected hip fracture. On\nthe doy of the accident, she was found at home, sitting down on the staircase in wet\n\nclothes and crying for help. Her neighbour tried to contact her son, but he was out of reach,\n\n50 finally the ambulance was called.\n\nOn admission, the patient had minimal injuries and only a few bruises on the right elbow.\nShe could ambulate without pain and her vital signs were normal. The imaging findings\nrulec out bone fractures, but osteopenia was noted in the raciograph. All results of her\nblood tests will be available tomorrow and will be forwarded to your practice so a\n\nIt should be noted that the MMSE score (22) revealed mild aged related dementia.\nTherefore, she requires attention from the Aged Care Assessment Team as home and\npersonal assistance might be necessary to prevent falls in the future. She would also benefit\nfrom further assessment of osteopenia.\n\nShould you have any further queries, please do not hesitate to contact me.\n\nYours sincerely,\nDoctor", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "Dear Doctor Smith,\nRe: Mrs. Sterra Fredrick, DOB 08/02/19\n\n| am writing to discharge one of your elderly patients back into your care. Mrs Frederick was\n\nadmitted to our Emergency Department following a fall and a suspected hip fracture. On\nthe doy of the accident, she was found at home, sitting down on the staircase in wet\n\nclothes and crying for help. Her neighbour tried to contact her son, but he was out of reach,\n\n50 finally the ambulance was called.\n\nOn admission, the patient had minimal injuries and only a few bruises on the right elbow.\nShe could ambulate without pain and her vital signs were normal. The imaging f